This work contains code and data derived from OpenMOPAC
(https://github.com/openmopac/mopac, Apache License 2.0, Copyright the MOPAC authors).
The derived parts are re-implementations in Python/PyTorch of algorithms in the MOPAC
23.2.5 Fortran sources, with the following changes:

  * Parameters: converted from models/parameters_for_PM6_C.F90 and
    parameters_for_PM7_C.F90 into PYSEQM's CSV format (seqm_pm7/params_pm6, params_pm7).
  * Core-core repulsion (integrals/ccrep.F90), PM7 "feathering" (mndod.F90: to_point),
    d-orbital two-centre integrals (mndod.F90: rijkl, charg, reppd2, rotatd incl. the
    method_PM7 block), Slater-Condon/EISOL terms (mndod.F90: scprm, eiscor;
    models/calpar.F90; integrals/sp_two_electron.F90), atom tables (models/parameters_C.F90),
    and the MM / dispersion / hydrogen-bond corrections (corrections/*.F90),
    rewritten as differentiable PyTorch code and applied to PYSEQM at import time.
  * New code not present in MOPAC: a general Slater-type-orbital overlap with
    analytic rotation (seqm_pm7/sto_overlap.py), and the patches that route
    PYSEQM's spd path through the above.

PYSEQM itself (https://github.com/lanl/PYSEQM) is used unmodified as a dependency.

The optional ozaki/ helper (oz2_shim.cu, build_oz2.sh) links against GEMMul8
(https://github.com/RIKEN-RCCS/GEMMul8, MIT License, Copyright (c) 2025- RIKEN R-CCS), which is downloaded at build time
and is not redistributed here.
